1
00:00:00,804 --> 00:00:01,934
(Leonard:)I don't know what to do.

2
00:00:02,105 --> 00:00:05,305
(Leonard:)The paper's terrible.
But if I tell her, she'll know that I read it...

3
00:00:05,542 --> 00:00:07,012
(Leonard:)...and she'll get really mad.

4
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:10,240
(Sheldon:)I was beating him so bad
he doesn't wanna be friends anymore.

5
00:00:10,447 --> 00:00:13,847
(Sheldon:)Why does everyone love me
except Stephen Hawking?

6
00:00:14,584 --> 00:00:17,614
(Leonard:)Is it possible we're having
two different conversations?

7
00:00:17,787 --> 00:00:20,087
(Sheldon:)How would I know?
I'm not listening to you.

8
00:00:21,624 --> 00:00:23,284
(Leonard:)Hang on.

9
00:00:24,661 --> 00:00:27,391
(Leonard:)Okay. Here's what we're gonna do.
Chess clock.

10
00:00:27,597 --> 00:00:29,967
(Leonard:)We each get five minutes
to talk about our problems.

11
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:33,333
(Leonard:)We'll take turns.
Each turn will consist of a statement...

12
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,970
(Leonard:)...and a helpful response from the friend.

13
00:00:36,172 --> 00:00:37,732
(Leonard:)Begin.

14
00:00:37,941 --> 00:00:40,911
(Sheldon:)I humiliated Stephen Hawking
in a game of "Words With Friends."

15
00:00:41,111 --> 00:00:43,741
(Sheldon:)He stopped playing.
And now we're not friends anymore.

16
00:00:44,314 --> 00:00:47,144
(Leonard:)He's probably busy.
You're worried about nothing.

17
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:49,650
(Leonard:)Give it a couple more days.
I'm sure he'll play...

18
00:00:49,819 --> 00:00:51,749
(Leonard:)...and you'll see that everything's fine.

19
00:00:51,921 --> 00:00:54,291
(Leonard:)My turn. I can't let Penny
hand in a bad paper...

20
00:00:54,457 --> 00:00:57,987
(Leonard:)...but how do I tell her it's bad
without letting her know that I read it?

21
00:00:58,228 --> 00:00:59,248
(Sheldon:)Hmm.

22
00:00:59,429 --> 00:01:02,019
(Sheldon:)Beats me. Now...

